WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:01.573
- Oh my God I love you.

00:00:01.573 --> 00:00:02.406
- [Kelly] Happy new year,

00:00:02.406 --> 00:00:03.267
I'm gonna to say that-
- Happy new year.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.190
- But I have to say this, it's so funny,

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.620
'cause on one of those times you're here,

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.350
my mom, I hadn't seen
the show that you're on,

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.610
and it was so funny
'cause you had mentioned

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:12.850
that somebody at American
Idol had said that you could,

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:13.760
they thought you were my mom.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.593
- Right.

00:00:14.593 --> 00:00:17.500
- My mom during Christmas
break, before new year,

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.557
literally said that she was like,

00:00:18.557 --> 00:00:20.510
"I saw someone with Valerie
Bertinelli the other day."

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:21.900
She was like, "I feel like
she could be your mom."

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.520
Which I think is weird
for your mom to say.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.353
- Yes.

00:00:25.353 --> 00:00:26.186
- Like my mom said it.

00:00:26.186 --> 00:00:28.180
But she was like, "I feel
like y'all look so similar."

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.820
And I was like, "That's so crazy!"

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:31.800
I was like, "We've had
this conversation before."

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.110
- I think I walked by
your mother after you won,

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.570
and she was sobbing as well.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.520
- Oh, sobbing.
- Yeah.

00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:37.353
- She was probably like,

00:00:37.353 --> 00:00:38.832
"Finally, we'll be able to pay bills."

00:00:38.832 --> 00:00:40.915
(laughs)

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.350
We're broke.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.700
Teachers don't make enough money.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:45.600
- No, they don't.

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.660
- They do not.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:48.300
And wait, one of the times
that we saw each other,

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.610
we were at a lunch and you
were talking about your son,

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:51.770
and how he's a musician,

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:53.440
you were so proud of him and,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:54.740
'cause it was big footsteps.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:55.960
- Yes.
- With his father, Eddie.

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.474
So it's amazing, he's
nominated for a Grammy.

00:00:58.474 --> 00:01:00.975
(shouting)
(applauding)

00:01:00.975 --> 00:01:01.808
Congratulations!

00:01:01.808 --> 00:01:03.550
- Thank you, thank you.

00:01:03.550 --> 00:01:06.210
I couldn't be more happy.

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:07.850
I'm so much more happy for his success,

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:09.750
than I ever, ever could be for mine.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:11.570
- Yeah, that's a mom.
- I'm over the moon.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.510
Yeah, I guess so.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:15.100
- How did you get the news
that he'd been nominated?

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:17.290
- I didn't realize the
nominations were happening

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:21.197
and it was online and I went,
"Oh my God I wanna see."

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:26.020
I saw Billie Eilish and she
was announcing the rock group.

00:01:26.020 --> 00:01:29.330
And when they got to the best song,

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:33.260
I screamed in the middle of
my bathroom all by myself,

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.910
scared my animals, they all
went running out of the room.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:38.410
But I mean, the first person
I wanted to call after Wolfie

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:43.360
was Ed, 'cause Ed was beyond
the moon, proud of Wolfie.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.800
He, the only thing in this world

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.400
that ever made Wolfie happy,

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.710
that ever made Ed happy,

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.298
they're the same person, was Wolfie.

00:01:51.298 --> 00:01:54.520
Ed just got so much joy
out of watching Wolfie

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:56.650
play music and be creative.

00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:59.960
And it's, I wish he was here.

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:01.640
- Well, and also, 'cause
it's one of those things,

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.020
when it's something you love and you see,

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.950
even when I see my daughter
at a school performance,

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.760
I'm not the mom that's like,

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:11.070
move your, make your smile,
honey, I'm not that mom,

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:14.290
but I do get excited 'cause
it's something that we share.

00:02:14.290 --> 00:02:15.380
- Yeah.
- So that's cool.

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.970
- It is.
- I'm so happy for him.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:17.803
Please tell him congratulations.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.380
- Thank you, I will.
- That's so fricking cool.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:20.213
- I will, thank you.
- Especially at songwriting,

00:02:20.213 --> 00:02:21.046
that's so cool.

00:02:21.046 --> 00:02:22.970
- You know how hard it is to write a song?

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.170
- It is, it is also, it's a hard category.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.340
There's so many amazing songs
that are released in a year.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:29.616
And how do you pick the few
that are gonna be in that,

00:02:29.616 --> 00:02:30.449
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:33.383
It's a hard thing, so, congratulations.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.580
Also, there's some sad news.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:37.300
I know that you were
really close with Betty,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.050
and I know that you worked
with her on "Hot in Cleveland"

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.740
and so, do you remember
the first time you met her?

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:45.990
- The first time I met
her, was at the reading,

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:48.640
the very first script reading
for "Hot in Cleveland"

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.150
and I was in awe.

00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:52.110
And when I, you've met Betty.

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:53.255
- I actually never met Betty.

00:02:53.255 --> 00:02:54.130
(gasps)

00:02:54.130 --> 00:02:55.040
- I can't believe that.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.610
- I never met Betty White.
- Oh my God.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.770
I know, and I'm such a huge fan, but yeah.

00:02:58.770 --> 00:02:59.603
Well who isn't.

00:02:59.603 --> 00:03:03.080
- When you're in her
presence, she literally glows.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:04.910
I'm telling you, I don't know how,

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:08.140
but the woman is just
a walking glow stick.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:11.750
Like she's just full of
gratitude and love and kindness.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:13.110
- Yeah.
- She was just

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:13.943
the greatest gift.
- And you've been

00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:15.210
in the industry for so long,

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.270
so y'all just met on "Hot in Cleveland.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:19.380
- Yeah, back.
- Are you still floored?

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:22.610
- Oh, yes, I mean,
Betty's been amazing for,

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:24.133
you know, 99 years.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:24.966
(chuckles)

00:03:24.966 --> 00:03:26.500
- I know I was so mad.

00:03:26.500 --> 00:03:29.430
'Cause I was like, really,
just shy of a hundred?

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:30.263
- That was, that was...

00:03:30.263 --> 00:03:31.096
- But that's Betty.

00:03:31.096 --> 00:03:32.750
Betty's got the best timing.

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.920
Why not send 2021 out with a bang?

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.440
Okay, see you later, I'm out.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.100
- She's like, peace! (laughs)

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.210
- So I couldn't help but notice

00:03:40.210 --> 00:03:43.790
that in your new lovely
book, it started here.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.060
Like after you were here.
- It did.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:46.750
We were right over there cooking,

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:48.020
making a crab and cheesy dip.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:49.332
- Which I don't cook well, but I love

00:03:49.332 --> 00:03:50.968
that it started there.
- You made that great dip.

00:03:50.968 --> 00:03:51.801
- Because of you.

00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:52.810
(both laugh)

00:03:52.810 --> 00:03:54.530
- And then, oh yes there we are,

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:56.390
and then I took the leftovers

00:03:56.390 --> 00:03:57.930
'cause I always have stuff at home too,

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.640
because I'm always
practicing before I do it.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:00.960
And I took it over to Wolfie's house

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.070
and that's when Ed came by and
it all starts the whole story

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.460
of this reconnection that Ed and I had

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:08.230
in the last few years of his life.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:09.680
- Oh, wow.
- Yeah.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:10.513
- That must have been hard,

00:04:10.513 --> 00:04:12.530
I know 'cause I've gone through a divorce,

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:15.316
still going through divorce and it feels,

00:04:15.316 --> 00:04:18.000
it's a weird thing, but
it feels like a death.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.370
It feels like such a
loss, divorce in general,

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.100
and then to lose him again,
that must've been really hard.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:23.933
- Yeah, it sucks.

00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:26.730
- 'Cause it's your kids'
father too, you know?

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:28.650
- Yeah, but there was something

00:04:28.650 --> 00:04:30.240
and I know so many people get mad at me

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.300
when I say that there was
a love that Ed and I had

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:35.230
that no one really can, but it's true,

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.161
I mean, I don't know why-

00:04:36.161 --> 00:04:37.930
- Why do they get mad, but
that's a beautiful thing?

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:40.080
- Because we were both
married to other people.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:42.550
But it wasn't, and it was nothing sexual.

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.383
It was nothing.

00:04:43.383 --> 00:04:46.400
It was just, I've known the
guy since I was 20 years old,

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:47.680
I was a baby.

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.090
And he was just my life
for a very long time.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.620
So I'm a little uncomfortable
talking about it,

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.890
but I'm not, because there's
nothing to be ashamed of

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:55.950
when you love somebody.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.070
- Yeah.
- Love is love.

00:04:57.070 --> 00:04:58.710
- I think there's room
to love a lot of people

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:00.430
and there are different types of love.

00:05:00.430 --> 00:05:01.263
- Yes.

00:05:01.263 --> 00:05:02.180
- Yeah.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.660
- And it turned into
like a brother, sister

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:07.770
and I care about him so
much, still do, still do.

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:09.860
- Why did you call the
book "Enough Already"?

00:05:09.860 --> 00:05:13.810
And it's, I love that "Learning
to love the way I am today".

00:05:13.810 --> 00:05:16.360
- Because I'm done.

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:17.730
I'm just done judging myself.

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:20.500
I'm done with all the negative
talk that I give to myself

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.220
because there's enough
negative talk out there.

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:23.680
It's just enough already, enough!

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.000
Enough getting on the scale,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.140
enough saying horrible
things about myself,

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:30.240
and just changing the
perspective, and changing

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.540
the view and the narrative.
- The narrative.

00:05:31.540 --> 00:05:32.373
- Thank you.

00:05:32.373 --> 00:05:35.400
And also I am enough, I'm enough.

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:36.530
- Yeah, and it's so.
- It's enough.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.230
- It's so interesting 'cause
from an outsider's perspective

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.530
and just even having the
one lunch we got to share,

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:43.750
it was like, I literally remember leaving

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.057
and telling Ashley, I was like,

00:05:45.057 --> 00:05:48.620
"Man, she is such a light,
she's so kind, she's so normal".

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.380
You were so cool, really...

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:51.440
- I thought the same thing about you.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:53.850
- Well, what's funny is
rarely do you meet people,

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.310
and I don't really.
- In this business.

00:05:55.310 --> 00:05:56.810
- We're always working and busy and busy

00:05:56.810 --> 00:05:59.420
and rarely do I really find that.

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.290
So it's so, I had advice
actually given to me for 2022

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:07.473
and it was, treat yourself
how you treat others,

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.710
'cause I feel like we are
kind to people a lot often

00:06:13.710 --> 00:06:15.280
more than to ourselves.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:17.210
- Yes, unfortunately.
- Which was so crappy!

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.240
- Right, and it's not okay!
- Why do we do that?

00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:20.640
- I don't know, I mean,
it's just I learned

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:23.460
from a very, very, very young
age by just the way you watch

00:06:23.460 --> 00:06:25.730
and the way you see the way
people treat each other.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:28.240
That it's just the certain
things that you're allowed to say

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:29.650
and not allowed to say
and not allowed to feel.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.846
And I learned at a young age

00:06:31.846 --> 00:06:35.580
that gaining weight was
unlovable, made me unlovable.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.413
- Wow.

00:06:36.413 --> 00:06:39.160
- So I'm still trying to
purge that out of my system

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.320
because it's not, that's
not true, it's just a lie.

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:43.930
- No, yeah, that's oh
my gosh that's so sad.

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.140
I think that's a thing in the
South that's said a lot too.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:47.140
I don't know if it's everywhere.

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:47.973
- All over the world.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.130
- It's definitely in the South,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:53.090
but I also, I think
what I am glad about is,

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:54.940
I think so many things
happened to me when I was young

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:58.050
about my weight that I
think even at a young age,

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:58.950
so many things get said

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:00.870
that I think that's
whenever I was just like,

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:02.810
whatever, I'm not gonna please anyone.

00:07:02.810 --> 00:07:04.390
- God bless you.
- I think I was lucky

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:06.920
it happened because before
I got in the industry,

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:08.910
'cause in industry you
were talking about your son

00:07:08.910 --> 00:07:11.270
being in the industry it's
very hard, even for men.

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:12.103
- Yes.

00:07:12.103 --> 00:07:13.500
- Even for men to look a certain way

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.706
and do a certain thing.

00:07:14.706 --> 00:07:16.510
And it's just such a silly thing.

00:07:16.510 --> 00:07:19.190
And I love the title "Enough Already".

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:22.410
'Cause it's very welcoming
to so many people

00:07:22.410 --> 00:07:24.370
that have the same fight within themself,

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:25.620
that they're trying to overcome.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:28.000
- It's hard when you
learn as a little girl

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:29.290
and then trying to get that out.

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.980
So for you to break that as a little girl

00:07:31.980 --> 00:07:33.310
is something to be really proud of.

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:34.290
It took me a long time.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.890
I mean, I watched my mom
not get loved by my dad

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:37.790
when she would gain weight.

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.940
I had an elementary school
teacher point at my belly

00:07:40.940 --> 00:07:42.050
and say, you better watch that.

00:07:42.050 --> 00:07:44.440
I didn't even realize I
had a body before that.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.730
Like I had no awareness
of what I looked like.

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:48.290
It was just, let's have fun.

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:49.230
And then all of a sudden I was like,

00:07:49.230 --> 00:07:51.480
oh, I'm supposed to look a certain way.

00:07:51.480 --> 00:07:52.313
Oh!

00:07:52.313 --> 00:07:53.850
- Yeah that's damaging.
- That's not okay.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:56.280
- Yeah, no, you gotta be so
careful with what you say

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.170
in front of the little
ones, they're sponges.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.210
And they retain everything, oh my gosh.

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.920
But you were married for 25 years

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.040
and something that I
love that you just said,

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:04.890
and I wanted to bring back.

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.380
'Cause I love that that
shared love can change,

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.500
it can be a different kind
of love, it can evolve.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.580
And I think that that's like gotta be

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:15.510
an elevated emotional kind of state.

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:17.350
Like I don't think a lot
of people can do that

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:20.240
and I love that you
loved in a different way.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.250
And I love that you've mentioned too

00:08:22.250 --> 00:08:24.250
that you still feel his presence.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:26.910
- I do, I do in so many different ways.

00:08:26.910 --> 00:08:29.280
There was a couple of things
in the book that I write about,

00:08:29.280 --> 00:08:32.320
really kind of woo-woo kind
of things that I'm like,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:34.550
if you believe in that
great, it happened to me.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:37.070
But there was something recently
that just happened to me

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.480
after I finished the book.

00:08:38.480 --> 00:08:42.620
And I had kind of like
made this pact with Ed

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.630
that I would see a certain bird

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:45.960
or was it two, or was it three?

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.650
I wasn't sure whether it
was two or three birds.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:50.170
And then I would know he was there.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:53.070
And so I was in the bathroom
early in the morning,

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:54.600
I had this big picture window and I said,

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:57.870
oh, there's three birds, Ed, are you here?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.150
I said, oh wait, was it two birds?

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.020
And I said, oh God, was it two or three?

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.060
So I don't know if it's you,
Ed, if you're here or not.

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:04.640
You know what, screw it, if you're here,

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.110
just send a whole flock of birds!

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.610
And literally, I didn't
even get that sentence

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:12.520
out of my mouth and a whole
flock of birds went going by.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:15.170
It must have been 20, 30
birds, these little tiny birds.

00:09:15.170 --> 00:09:17.430
And you know, they do
those waves, you see them.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.490
That's what happened, went
by, never saw the birds again.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.400
I'm like, okay, I got goosebumps.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.330
It's like, oh Ed, okay cool, you're here.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.163
- And here's the thing too,

00:09:25.163 --> 00:09:26.670
who cares if people
believe or don't believe.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:27.810
You believe and it happened.

00:09:27.810 --> 00:09:29.360
- It made me happy.
- You had that pact with him

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:30.951
and it's special, yeah.

00:09:30.951 --> 00:09:33.380
I'll tell you what, I've
never seen anything,

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.620
but I will say my child,
my daughter, River,

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:38.670
whenever she was a baby,
no lights were in the room,

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.710
there was nothing on,

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:40.770
it's not like she was staring at anything.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:42.960
It was a pitch black room.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:44.050
I had the white noise going,

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.770
so they'd go to sleep.
- I love that.

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.200
- Yes, and then I had her in,

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:51.230
and she legit was sitting
there smiling, giggling,

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:52.640
just laughing at something.

00:09:52.640 --> 00:09:55.870
And I was like, I literally
said the same thing out loud.

00:09:55.870 --> 00:09:58.620
I was like, so I don't know
if anyone's here right now,

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.880
but if you are just be kind
to my child, whoever you are.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:05.210
And then I was like, and
you're cool, you can hang out.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:07.500
I literally had a conversation
with maybe nothing,

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.970
but I was like, just on the off chance

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:11.466
she's talking to someone.

00:10:11.466 --> 00:10:13.380
- Just be nice.
- Yes, just be nice.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.100
Don't scare the crap out
of her is all I'm asking.

00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:15.970
- And she was smiling so it's good.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:18.500
- She was though, she was so intensely

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:21.770
having a moment with
something and I've never felt

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:23.150
I've never had anything
like that happen to me,

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:24.527
but it was really weird.

00:10:24.527 --> 00:10:26.470
- There's really cool
things I write about,

00:10:26.470 --> 00:10:27.860
a couple of things that
I write about in the book

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.640
about more instances where it's like,

00:10:29.640 --> 00:10:32.070
okay, thanks Ed, can you just
give me a break right now?

00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:33.670
- Yeah, we all our energy, just saying.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:34.503
- Yes, yes.

00:10:34.503 --> 00:10:35.336
- Yes.

00:10:35.336 --> 00:10:36.580
- And our energy needs to go somewhere.

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:38.300
- It's still here, I like it.

00:10:38.300 --> 00:10:40.676
We could keep talking, but
my producer's gonna kill me.

00:10:40.676 --> 00:10:41.890
(laughs)

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:43.087
Mark, look, I love her.

